---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What data Insider Trades does and does not collect."
>
  <div class="static-page">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: 2026</p>

    <p>
      Insider Trades is a static website. It has no user accounts, login, or
      comment system, and it does not ask you for personal information.
    </p>

    <h2>Server logs</h2>
    <p>
      The site is served by GitHub Pages. Like most web hosts, the hosting
      provider automatically records standard request data — such as your IP
      address, browser user-agent, and the pages requested — for security and to
      operate the service. We do not control the retention of those logs and do
      not use them to identify individuals.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We may use a privacy-focused analytics tool to count page views and
      referrers in aggregate. If enabled, it will not use cookies to track you
      across other websites. This page will be updated to name the tool in use.
    </p>

    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>
      If third-party advertising is shown on the site, ad providers may set
      cookies or use similar technologies to serve and measure ads, potentially
      based on your visits to this and other sites. You can usually control ad
      personalisation through your browser settings and through tools such as the
      ad-industry opt-out pages. See our <a href="/disclosure/">Disclosure</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>External links</h2>
    <p>
      Briefs link to the underlying filings on SEC EDGAR, and some pages may
      contain affiliate links. Once you follow a link to another site, this
      policy no longer applies; review that site's own privacy policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about privacy, or a request related to your data, can be sent to
      <a href="mailto:naka.kn007@gmail.com">naka.kn007@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
